//RS /// #2010 / #2011 — store then replay real example stems: run 2 must match run 1
//RS /// byte for byte on stdout, stderr AND exit code.
//RS ///
//RS /// Exit code is the load-bearing column. Every other warm-hit fixture in this
//RS /// file is a tiny inline program that exits 0, which is exactly why a warm hit
//RS /// that had forgotten its entry was fallible — rendering the error and still
//RS /// exiting 0 — stayed invisible for the whole life of the cache.
//RS ///
//RS /// The matrix is stems, not inline strings, because the shapes that break a
//RS /// replay are shapes inline fixtures never had: a generator, a `#CLI` typed
//RS /// entry, an unhandled `Err` at the program edge.
//RS #[test]
